        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70720,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rete testis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70721,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients generally present with a unilateral painless mass, or the tumour is found incidentally in an orchiectomy specimen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70722,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rete testis adenomas are rare, with &lt;&nbsp;15&nbsp;well-described cases {11202545; 15502808; 32619438}. They affect a wide age range (12&ndash;79&nbsp;years).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70723,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70724,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70725,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are circumscribed cystic, mixed cystic/solid, or solid lesions in the mediastinal (hilar) aspect of the testis {11202545; 15502808; 32619438}. They range from 10&nbsp;to 55&nbsp;mm in diameter.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70726,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 172,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most of the tumours are cystadenomas composed of variably sized dilated cystic spaces lined by cuboidal to low columnar cells, sometimes ciliated, with bland nuclear features {11202545; 15502808; 32619438}. Transition from normal rete testis epithelium is helpful for diagnosis. The cystic spaces may merge imperceptibly with background rete glands. The epithelium may be stratified with areas of tufting or budding. Papillary structures can be present within cystic spaces {4468259; 7062394; 10320920}. There may be prominent fibrous stroma; such cases are often referred to as cystadenofibromas {32619438}. Occasionally, solid lesions composed of elongated tubules embedded in a fibrous stroma may be seen {3364196}. No atypia or infiltration of adjacent testis is present and mitoses are rare.</p>\r\n<p>The tumour formerly known as sertoliform cystadenoma of the rete testis is now considered a Sertoli cell tumour arising in the rete testis (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/147\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Sertoli cell tumour</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
